  "hints": [
    "Each time you find a land cell you have not visited yet, you have found a new island. How do you make sure you never count that island's other cells again?",
    "Scan every cell. On unvisited land, add 1 to the count, then flood-fill: visit every land cell reachable up, down, left or right (with a stack or a queue) and mark it as seen.",
    "The paint-bucket tool in an image editor is the same flood fill: it spreads to every neighbouring pixel of the same colour."
  ],
